# Accent Across: LA electro on the 808 the way Egyptian Lover describes
# making his sound (Spin, 2026): the accent "all the way across to make
# everything louder", then "EQ it and take the bass out", and "all the
# reverbs, all the delays". An original tune in that style, not his.
# The 808 is the sample pack (make samples), its pads by number: p1 rimshot,
# p2 snare, p3 clap, p4 claves, p5 maracas, p6 closed hat, p7 low conga,
# p8 cowbell, p9 low tom, p10 open hat, p11 mid tom, p12 mid conga,
# p13 cymbal, p14 high tom, p15 high conga.
# On the sample kit an accent (X) is velocity 1 against a hit's 0.75: the
# intro plays plain hits, then every hit is accented from the groove on.
# The 808's strip: the Eq insert's low shelf (200 Hz) down 12 dB, a
# compressor for the hot desk, echo and reverb.
# The melody is in E phrygian dominant (E F G# A B C D).
tempo 125
swing 52
scale e phrygian-dominant

setting bass = Sh101 Sh101Bass
setting lead = Sh101 Sh101Lead
setting stab = Juno106 JunoPoly: AdsrAttack 0.002, AdsrDecay 0.16, AdsrSustain 0, AdsrRelease 0.12, Cutoff 2200, Resonance 0.3, EnvCutoff 0.5, FenvDecay 0.12

track tr808 drums PadSampler
samples tr808 roland-tr808
track bass synth bass
track lead synth lead
track stab synth stab

# Send1 echo, Send2 reverb
strip tr808: Level 0.85, I1Type Eq, I1A 0.1, I2Type Comp, I2A 0.6, Send1 0.25, Send2 0.3
strip bass: Level 0.75
strip lead: Level 0.45, Pan 0.2, Send1 0.45, Send2 0.4
strip stab: Level 0.35, Pan -0.25, Send1 0.3, Send2 0.5
# P1 a dotted eighth at 125 (0.36 s), P2 a big plate
master: MasterGain 0.75, P1Return 0.5, EchoTime 0.36, EchoFeedback 0.5, P2Return 0.45, ReverbSize 3.5

# the 808, plain hits: the kick off the beat, clap on two and four, the
# hats on the sixteenths, the cowbell's figure
clip plain = tr808 /16
  bd x.....x...x.....
  p3 ....x.......x...
  p6 x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  p8 x..x..x...x..x..x..x..x...x.x...
clip across = tr808 /16
  bd X.....X...X..X..X.....X...X.....
  p3 ....X.......X...
  p2 ....X.......X..X
  p6 XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
  p10 ..............X.
  p8 X..X..X...X..X..X..X..X...X.X...
  p1 ..X....X......X.
  p4 X..X..X...X.X...
  p5 XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
# the clap in a roll into the next bar, toms down the kit, the cymbal on one
clip roll = tr808 /16
  bd X.....X...X.....
  p3 ....X.......X3X3X4X4
  p6 XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
  p14 ........X.X.....
  p11 ..........X.X...
  p9 ............X.X.
  p13 X...............
# congas and rimshots under the echo, no kick
clip conga = tr808 /16
  p7 X.....X...X.....
  p12 ...X......X..X..
  p15 .X.X....X....X.X
  p1 ..X.....X.....X.
  p5 XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
  p3 ....X.......X...

# bass: E with the flat second and the third, the 808 kick's rhythm
clip bassline = bass
  "<[e1! ~ ~ e1 ~ ~ e2 ~ e1! ~ ~ e1 ~ f1 ~ e1] [e1! ~ ~ e1 ~ ~ e2 ~ g#1 ~ a1 ~ g#1 ~ f1 ~]>"
# lead: the flat second falling back to the root, an answer climbing to C
clip theme = lead
  "<[e4 ~ f4 e4 ~ ~ g#4 ~ a4 g#4 f4 ~ e4 ~ ~ ~] [~ ~ b4 c5 b4 ~ a4 g#4 a4 ~ g#4 f4 e4 ~ ~ ~] [e5 ~ d5 c5 b4 ~ c5 b4 a4 ~ g#4 ~ f4 g#4 e4 ~] [~ ~ ~ ~ f4 ~ e4 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~]>"
# stab: E major with the flat second over it, on the off-beats
clip stabs = stab
  "<[~ [e3,g#3,b3] ~ ~ ~ [e3,g#3,b3] ~ ~] [~ [f3,a3,c4] ~ ~ ~ [e3,g#3,b3] ~ ~]>"

scene intro 4: plain
scene groove 8: across bassline
scene theme 8: across bassline theme stabs
scene roll 2: roll bassline
scene conga 8: conga bassline stabs
scene theme_b 8: across bassline theme stabs
scene outro 4: across stabs
arrange intro groove theme roll conga theme_b roll outro
